 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Tool input validation: `ToolRegistry.execute` now automatically validates inputs against a tool's
+  declared `inputSchema` using a JSON Schema validator (`ajv`). A malformed call returns a
+  rejection `ToolResponse` to the model instead of invoking the executor, allowing the AI to
+  correct and retry within its turn budget. Rejection messages redact property values to prevent
+  sensitive data leakage. Static tool schemas are validated and compiled at registration time.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **Breaking (Minor)**: Tool executors no longer receive malformed input. If an executor relied on seeing
+  input that violates its schema to produce its own error message, it will no longer be invoked; the
+  generic validation error is returned to the model instead. Type casting input fields is still
+  recommended for TypeScript, but manual checks for `required` properties can be removed from
+  executors whose schemas already declare them.
+
